# Gap-lane / autoteach window — Bonsai 256 v4 (minted 2026-08-17).
#
# 256 ids drawn from the model's OWN vocabulary via tools/gen_window_candidates
# (16735 qualifying word tokens), taking the highest-ranked entries not already
# excluded. Excluded: ledger-closed ids (gaps.txt status=2, the same rule
# bin/gap_inject applies), inbox-pending ids, and every id in v1/v2/v3.
# Verified fresh: `gap_inject --dry-run` reports remaining=248 of 256.
#
# Unlike v2/v3, which drew raw vocab ids and landed on fragments (Ġ%, .as,
# pir), v4 uses the curated word-token pool — the same basis as v1 — so the
# entries are real high-frequency words (Ġthat, Ġreturn, Ġclass).
#
# Deliberately window-only: this file does NOT pin CNET_TEACHER_HTTP /
# CNET_RESIDUAL_HTTP the way cnet-gap-window-v3.env does. The teacher endpoint
# is an independent decision (v3 pinned :8080, the CPU llama-server, while the
# GPU one runs on :8081) and should not ride along with a window swap.
CNET_WINDOW_FILE=/home/marble/AI/CNET/english_window_256_bonsai_v4.txt
CNET_RESIDUAL_WINDOW=/home/marble/AI/CNET/english_window_256_bonsai_v4.txt
